# Control Plane services may project state and issue commands.
user control-plane
topic readwrite homeplatform/v1/#

# The first deployed Node can publish only its own state and receive only its
# own Desired State and command requests. Add a matching explicit block when a
# new credential is created; do not grant topic wildcards across Nodes.
user macbook
topic write homeplatform/v1/nodes/macbook/#
topic write homeplatform/v1/services/macbook/#
topic write homeplatform/v1/events/#
topic write homeplatform/v1/telemetry/macbook/#
topic write homeplatform/v1/commands/macbook/result
topic read homeplatform/v1/config/desired-state/#
topic read homeplatform/v1/commands/macbook/request

# Health checks have no application privileges.
user healthcheck
topic read $SYS/broker/uptime

# The native kiosk controller owns only its directly attached Arduino and
# publishes its state/input. It cannot read commands for unrelated Nodes.
user kiosk-controller
topic read homeplatform/v1/alerts/current
topic write homeplatform/v1/nodes/__KIOSK_NODE_ID__/#
topic write homeplatform/v1/devices/kiosk/#
